{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md | sed -n '100,160p'\"","aggregated_output":"   100\tspecified here.\n   101\t\n   102\t```clojure\n   103\t(gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify   verify\n   104\t       :dao.stream.middleware/decision h})\n   105\t```\n   106\t\n   107\tThe decision medium is written by an interpreter the composition runs over\n   108\tits fact streams (the index): it folds facts with its own cursors, at its\n   109\town cadence, and appends each derived decision. Neither the gate nor the\n   110\tindex knows of the other; the medium is their only coupling.\n   111\t\n   112\t`wrap` calls `cursor` with `:dao.stream/oldest` once when it constructs\n   113\tthe gate. The decision medium must be open, readable and complete-retention;\n   114\tif cursor minting is not `ok`, that gate starts unavailable and retries\n   115\tcursor minting once on each operation. A successful mint is its read\n   116\tcursor. The medium has capacity one and evicts its older value.\n   117\t\n   118\tOn each operation, the gate calls `next` once at its read cursor. On `ok`,\n   119\tit stores the successor cursor and value. On `blocked`, it keeps the cursor\n   120\tand last value. On `end`, it clears the value and becomes ended. On `gap`,\n   121\tit clears the value, adopts the recovery cursor, and calls `next` once more.\n   122\tIf that call is `ok`, it stores the successor and value; if `blocked`, it\n   123\tkeeps the recovery cursor without a value; if `end`, it becomes ended; if\n   124\t`gap`, it adopts that recovery cursor and remains without a value. It does\n   125\tnot read a third time in this operation. On any other non-`ok` outcome, it\n   126\tclears the value and retries cursor minting at the next operation.\n   127\t\n   128\t`verify` receives the last value observed, or\n   129\t`{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}` when there is none. That value is a\n   130\tbounded snapshot, not a promise that it is the newest concurrent write.\n   131\t`nil` passes the request through; a reason short-circuits with\n   132\t`:dao.stream/refused` and `:dao.stream.middleware/reason`. A policy that\n   133\tmust fail closed refuses the marker. The cursor and value are state of the\n   134\twrapped handle, supplied to `wrap`, not global state. The composition must\n   135\tserialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock or wait.\n   136\tThe decision medium is not the wrapped stream, so the position rule on the\n   137\tinner handle is untouched.\n   138\t\n   139\tA gate that must account for its own decisions appends each as\n   140\t`{:dao.stream.middleware/decision :allow | :refuse ...}` to a side stream\n   141\tit was composed with: this is **decision emission**, and an index that\n   142\tobserves that stream is how metered use keeps its state on a stream\n   143\trather than in the gate.\n   144\t\n   145\t**present**, the credential step.\n   146\t\n   147\t```clojure\n   148\t(present {:dao.stream.middleware/present (fn [ctx req] -> credential)})\n   149\t```\n   150\t\n   151\tIts `in` associates the result under `:dao.stream.remote/credential`. Its\n   152\t`out` is identity.\n   153\t\n   154\tNeither middleware knows what a credential is. The trivial policy this\n   155\trepository ships with is an allow-list keyed on `:dao.stream.remote/channel`\n   156\tin `ctx`, ignoring the credential. Everything else belongs to\n   157\t[`dao.shibi.md`](./dao.shibi.md).\n   158\t\n   159\t## Exemplars\n   160\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
