{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '560,620p';\"","aggregated_output":"   560\tits lease intact. Expiry is a present answer, the `not-found` error, on a\n   561\thealthy channel. Only expiry frees anything. A meeting peer that restarts\n   562\tloses its table and ledger, so every pair is gone, holders observe\n   563\t`not-found` and re-propose; this is `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant\n   564\twith an empty inventory, correct because the table is process-scoped.\n   565\t\n   566\tUnits are the composition's; these conventions fix `{:ms 1 :s 1000}`.\n   567\t\n   568\t## 7. Middleware and the ShiBi seam\n   569\t\n   570\tThe mechanism is `dao.stream.middleware.md`: a middleware is a map of two\n   571\tpure transforms over the operation map and the outcome map; `wrap` turns a\n   572\thandle and a chain into a handle on the same logical stream; a middleware\n   573\tmaps position `p` of the inner to position `p` of the outer and never\n   574\ttouches a cursor, an anchor, an identity, an id or an outcome kind. This\n   575\tdocument adds the network attachment points: the **table entry** (the\n   576\tserved handle, before it enters the table; the mirror sees only the wrapped\n   577\thandle; gating, value encryption for serving, redaction, metering), the\n   578\t**reflection** (inside the host-composed attach closure; presenting a\n   579\tcredential, value decryption, metering), and the **channel** (reserved for\n   580\ta channel-level wrapper, deferred below).\n   581\t\n   582\tKeys and chains are composition data handed to `wrap`, never descriptor\n   583\tfields. Value-level encryption hides values and leaves identity, ops,\n   584\tcursors, sizes and timing visible. **Channel-level encryption is deferred:\n   585\tthis version specifies no wrapper at the channel attachment point**, its\n   586\tinterface and its ordering against codec and fragmentation (encode, then\n   587\tencrypt, then fragment) being requirements on that future design, not a\n   588\tdesign here. The exact consequence: a relay peer that carries requests and\n   589\tanswers sees every envelope in the clear, identities, ops, cursors, ids,\n   590\tsizes and timing included, and any part of a value not hidden by composed\n   591\tvalue-level middleware. Key distribution is a convention and is not\n   592\tspecified here. Ciphers come from libraries.\n   593\t\n   594\tThe capability-agnostic seam has an opaque per-request\n   595\t`:dao.stream.remote/credential` key, mirror-supplied channel context, a\n   596\tmirror-side gate, and reflection-side `present`; refusal is\n   597\t`:dao.stream/refused`. No token format or verification policy is specified.\n   598\tThe gate consumes a bounded decision published by an index interpreter.\n   599\t`dao.shibi.md` states the limit: `verify` is the adapter contract for a\n   600\tquery interpreter over that decision snapshot, not a general tuple-space\n   601\tquery engine. General query execution and request-specific result delivery\n   602\tare deferred to ShiBi; no new wire shape is required.\n   603\t\n   604\tLease attribution uses per-author media and needs no credential. A gate on\n   605\ta renewal medium is an optional composition.\n   606\t\n   607\t## 8. Unification and contract boundary\n   608\t\n   609\t`dao.stream.remote` replaces `dao.stream.serve.md` and succeeds\n   610\t`dao.jing.remote` whole; the successor path and the fate of each existing\n   611\tnetwork mechanism are recorded in\n   612\t[`dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md`](./dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md).\n   613\tThe only `dao.stream.md` changes are the five amendments listed there;\n   614\tthey add no network or capability concept to the contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
