{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md | sed -n '198,270p'; git diff -- docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md | tail -100\"","aggregated_output":"   198\t  vocabulary beside its older deposit-model wording, and `dao.stream.md`'s\n   199\t  own Close-section \"server-side accepted-connection handle\", track the\n   200\t  contract's wording and are re-worded with the code slices, not before.\n   201\t\n   202\t## 5. Unification: the fate of every existing path\n   203\t\n   204\tMoved from the spec's section 8, which keeps only the normative summary.\n   205\tEvery existing network path, verified against the tree, and its fate:\n   206\t\n   207\t- `dao.stream.ws` and the jvm, node, browser, dart adapters: **subsumed**.\n   208\t  Already a channel: writer plus deposit medium plus the spec's 3.1\n   209\t  projection. Its accept and disclaim frames and served-path table become\n   210\t  unnecessary once `not-found` is an answer per identity; retiring them is\n   211\t  slice 3.\n   212\t- `dao.stream.serving`: **retired**. Forwards a source into every accepted\n   213\t  socket and flattens a source `gap` into a detach: the copy model. Its\n   214\t  consumers are `yin.repl.serve` and `dao.jing.remote` (which requires and\n   215\t  drives it); both are retired by slices 4 and 5.\n   216\t- `dao.stream.forward`: **unrelated**. A local copy step; replication by\n   217\t  convention, not exposure.\n   218\t- `dao.stream.rpc`: **convention-over**. Correlation by id over two streams\n   219\t  is the spec's section 5 service; its state machine may be kept as one\n   220\t  such vocabulary over reflections, or retired in slice 5.\n   221\t- `dao.stream.rpc.ws`: **retired**. Its only job is translating `:ws/`\n   222\t  envelopes for rpc; the 3.1 projection is the channel binding now.\n   223\t- `dao.stream.apply` as a wire envelope: **retired**. Its ok-or-error\n   224\t  wrapper duplicates the outcome map. The `:dao.stream.apply/call` AST node\n   225\t  and the VM's FFI bridge keep the name and are unrelated to the network.\n   226\t- `yin.repl.serve`, `connect`, `driver`, `adapter`, the `daostream:ws://`\n   227\t  URL: **convention-over**. An eval service: `requests` and `answers`\n   228\t  streams, `:op/eval` as payload; the URL becomes a remote descriptor for\n   229\t  that pair. The shared-shell privilege is its interpreter's policy.\n   230\t- `dao.jing.remote`, `remote.step`, `remote.async`, the `:dao.jing/remote`\n   231\t  coordinate in `dao.jing.coordinate`: **retired**. Deprecated whole;\n   232\t  replaced by `dao.jing.content` (section 1).\n   233\t- `yin.repl.link`, `yin.vm.linker` M3 and M4: **convention-over**. The\n   234\t  content pair is a request and response service over reflections or local\n   235\t  ring buffers; the linker's stepped core is unchanged.\n   236\t- `dao.data.btree.storage/hydrate-async`, `store-tree-async`:\n   237\t  **convention-over**. Consume the content client of section 1; the\n   238\t  callback facade is host policy, per `dao.stream.md` OD-5.\n   239\t- `dao.jing.dht.node` UDP DHT: **unrelated**. Raw JVM datagram RPC with its\n   240\t  own Kademlia envelope; its socket rules and 1200-byte budget are the UDP\n   241\t  channel's template.\n   242\t- `dao.stream.transit`, `dao.stream.cbor`: **subsumed**. The channel\n   243\t  codecs, unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
