{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md | sed -n '105,165p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.shibi.md | sed -n '18,65p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '590,605p'; git diff --check; git diff --unified=0 -- docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md docs/design/dao.shibi.md docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md | awk '/\"'^'\"\\\\+[\"'^+]/ { line=substr($0,2); if (length(line)>80) print \"WIDE \" length(line) \":\" line; if (line ~ /[''^ -~]/) print \"NONASCII:\" line }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md | sed -n '105,165p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.shibi.md | sed -n '18,65p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '590,605p'; git diff --check; git diff --unified=0 -- docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md docs/design/dao.shibi.md docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md | awk '/\"'^'\"\\\\+[\"'^+]/ { line=substr($0,2); if (length(line)>80) print \"WIDE \" length(line) \":\" line; if (line ~ /[''^ -~]/) print \"NONASCII:\" line }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"     599 docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md\n   105\t```\n   106\t\n   107\tThe decision medium is written by an interpreter the composition runs over\n   108\tits fact streams (the index): it folds facts with its own cursors, at its\n   109\town cadence, and appends each derived decision. Neither the gate nor the\n   110\tindex knows of the other; the medium is their only coupling. A decision is\n   111\twhatever value the index publishes; the gate reads none of it. It may be an\n   112\timmutable query value, a relation value or an opened published index, in\n   113\twhich case `verify` is a query over it with the request as bindings: the\n   114\tshape `dao.space.query/q` has (a query over immutable inputs, opening\n   115\tnothing), and the required adapter contract for a query interpreter that\n   116\tplugs into the gate (`dao.shibi.md`, How it plugs in).\n   117\t\n   118\t`wrap` calls `cursor` with `:dao.stream/oldest` once when it constructs\n   119\tthe gate. The medium must be open and readable; it has capacity one and\n   120\tevicts its older value. If cursor minting is not `ok`, the gate has no read\n   121\tcursor or decision. Each operation retries `cursor` once; if it is still\n   122\tnot `ok`, `next` is skipped and `verify` receives the none marker. A\n   123\tsuccessful mint is its read cursor.\n   124\t\n   125\tOn each operation, the gate calls `next` once at its read cursor. On `ok`,\n   126\tit stores the successor cursor and value. On `blocked`, it keeps the cursor\n   127\tand last value. On `end`, it clears the value and becomes ended. On `gap`,\n   128\tit clears the value, adopts the recovery cursor, and calls `next` once more.\n   129\tIf that call is `ok`, it stores the successor and value; if `blocked`, it\n   130\tkeeps the recovery cursor without a value; if `end`, it becomes ended; if\n   131\t`gap`, it adopts that recovery cursor and remains without a value. It does\n   132\tnot read a third time in this operation. On any other non-`ok` outcome,\n   133\tit clears the value and cursor, then retries cursor minting next operation.\n   134\t\n   135\t`verify` receives the last value observed, or\n   136\t`{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}` when there is none, or\n   137\t`{:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}` once the gate is ended (the medium\n   138\tclosed; no later operation reads). That value is a bounded snapshot, not a\n   139\tpromise that it is the newest concurrent write.\n   140\t`nil` passes the request through; a reason short-circuits with\n   141\t`{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   142\t:dao.stream.middleware/reason reason}`. A policy that must fail closed\n   143\trefuses the marker. The cursor and value are state of the\n   144\twrapped handle, supplied to `wrap`, not global state. The composition must\n   145\tserialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock or wait.\n   146\tThe decision medium is not the wrapped stream, so the position rule on the\n   147\tinner handle is untouched.\n   148\t\n   149\tA gate that must account for its own decisions appends each as\n   150\t`{:dao.stream.middleware/decision :allow | :refuse ...}` to a side stream\n   151\tit was composed with: this is **decision emission**, and an index that\n   152\tobserves that stream is how metered use keeps its state on a stream\n   153\trather than in the gate.\n   154\t\n   155\t**present**, the credential step.\n   156\t\n   157\t```clojure\n   158\t(present {:dao.stream.middleware/present (fn [ctx req] -> credential)})\n   159\t```\n   160\t\n   161\tIts `in` associates the result under `:dao.stream.remote/credential`. Its\n   162\t`out` is identity.\n   163\t\n   164\tNeither middleware knows what a credential is. The trivial policy this\n   165\trepository ships with is an allow-list keyed on `:dao.stream.remote/channel`\n    18\t## How it plugs in\n    19\t\n    20\tShiBi integrates through the middleware seam of\n    21\t[`dao.stream.middleware.md`](./dao.stream.middleware.md) and the attachment\n    22\tpoints of [`dao.stream.remote.md`](./dao.stream.remote.md) section 7, which\n    23\tare fixed and which ShiBi must not change. The fit to two interpreters is\n    24\tthis, and it is the one path this version chooses:\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Its index interpreter** observes ShiBi's fact streams (grants,\n    27\t  caveats, revocations, emitted decisions) with its own cursors,\n    28\t  materializes them as `dao.space.index` materializes covered indexes, and\n    29\t  publishes the resulting immutable query value, a relation value or an\n    30\t  opened published index, as the decision onto the gate's capacity-1\n    31\t  decision medium (`dao.stream.middleware.md`, gate). The value published\n    32\t  is the tuple space's state at that moment.\n    33\t- **Its query interpreter is `verify`**, and `verify` is the required\n    34\t  adapter contract: a pure function of one immutable query value, the\n    35\t  context and the request, evaluating ShiBi's authorization rules as a\n    36\t  Datalog query with the request as bindings, the shape\n    37\t  `dao.space.query/q` already has (a query over immutable inputs, opening\n    38\t  nothing), and answering nil or a reason.\n    39\t- **A `present`**, a pure function of context and request that produces\n    40\t  the value carried in `:dao.stream.remote/credential`.\n    41\t- **A reason vocabulary** under its own namespace for\n    42\t  `:dao.stream.middleware/reason`.\n    43\t- **Where use is metered**, the decision facts the gate emits, which the\n    44\t  index observes like any other fact stream.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Limits of the adapter contract**, stated precisely. `verify` runs\n    47\tsynchronously inside one operation on one snapshot: its cost per operation\n    48\tis bounded by the composition, and a query over an opened published index\n    49\tresolves only what is already local, because `verify` opens, fetches and\n    50\twaits for nothing; a rule that would need a remote read is a rule the index\n    51\tmust have materialized. Its input is the latest published snapshot, so a\n    52\tgrant or revocation is effective only once the index has observed and\n    53\tpublished it: staleness is bounded by the index's cadence and the medium's\n    54\teviction, and a policy that must fail closed does so on the `none` marker\n    55\tand the `ended` marker. A decision is per call and is not itself a fact\n    56\tunless the gate emits it.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Non-goal in this version.** Request-specific decisions published through\n    59\tordinary streams, the query interpreter reading requests off a stream and\n    60\tappending one decision per request for the gate to await, are not\n    61\tspecified: a gate awaiting a per-request answer would wait, and no\n    62\toperation waits. If a later ShiBi needs that path it is an addition beside\n    63\t`verify`, not a change to it.\n    64\t\n    65\tThe contract's refusal outcome is `:dao.stream/refused` and is\n   590\t\n   591\tLease attribution uses per-author media; renewal gates are optional.\n   592\t\n   593\t## 8. Unification\n   594\t`dao.jing.content` succeeds `dao.jing.remote` whole. The implementation\n   595\tplan lists the successor vocabulary and network-path fates.\n   596\t\n   597\t## 9. Contract boundary\n   598\t\n   599\tFive `dao.stream.md` amendments (plan 2) add no network or capability concepts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-26 21:28:18 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 04:28:18 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n1. **Decision reads:** Specified initial `:oldest` cursor acquisition and retry, every `next` outcome, one recovery read after `gap`, repeated-gap handling, and composition-serialized calls without middleware waits or locks. [dao.stream.middleware.md:107–147](docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md)\n\n2. **ShiBi fit:** Chose the bounded adapter contract: the index publishes an immutable tuple-space snapshot, and `verify` runs the query with the request as bindings. General request-specific decisions over streams are explicitly deferred, with the reasons and limits stated. [dao.shibi.md:23–63](docs/design/dao.shibi.md) [dao.stream.remote.md:580–589](docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md)\n\n3. **Spec length:** Moved path fates and the amendment inventory into the implementation plan; the remote spec keeps a short unification and contract-boundary summary. Final `dao.stream.remote.md` length: **599 lines**. [dao.stream.remote.md:593–599](docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md) [implementation-plan.md:56–62, 178–219](docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md)\n\n4. **Historical content path:** Marked the old `default-handlers` / `connect-content!` instructions historical and pointed to planned `dao.jing.content`. [docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md:242–247](docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md)\n\n5. **Pair-channel gap:** Specified that an `in` gap terminates that link; the link reports abandoned append effects as unknown, and reattachment uses the same pair descriptor with a fresh `:newest` cursor. [dao.stream.remote.md:400–410](docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md)\n\n`git diff --check` passed; added lines checked for ASCII and an 80-column maximum. No tests were run.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE"}}
